# What a diff-reviewer rubric proposal job may do: read its repository's proposal job and submit
# the proposed rubric to the platform, and read GitHub. It reaches no review job and no pull
# request on the platform, and posts nothing to GitHub. An operator accepts or rejects what it
# proposes on the platform.
#
# The account is the platform's agent token, the same one the `reviewer` spec names (see there).
#
# Which repository is the task's: the platform queues a proposal job through its second orchestra
# client (`diff-reviewer-proposer.json`) with an `upstream` and no `issue_number`, and orchestra
# states it as `task_upstream(owner, name)` in the token's authority block. The proposal routes
# carry no `pull` fact, so the binding is to the repository alone; the platform binds the request
# to the repository's live proposal job.
spec rubric-proposer
  description "Proposes a review rubric for one repository, for the diff-reviewer platform."
  max_ttl 24h

  account diff-reviewer/agent
    allow propose
    datalog '''
      check if repository($o, $n), task_upstream($o, $n);
    '''

  grant orchestra-reviewer-github
